// Vitest Snapshot v1, https://vitest.dev/guide/snapshot.html

exports[`buildBulkPrompt > is byte-identical to the pre-selection output 1`] = `
"Replace 6 non-FOSS items with FOSS alternatives

## what
For every item listed under \`## known\`, research FOSS alternatives, suggest the best one, then install it unless the item is marked research only (firmware blobs, Steam library entries).
## where
This Arch Linux machine. Scanner and curated verdicts: ~/src/foss-audit (data/curated.json).
## must
- Work one item at a time, in the order listed: steps 0 and 1 for an item, then wait for my pick before step 2.
- 0. research: find the current FOSS options for it (pacman, AUR, flatpak, upstream), including the curated ones listed for it. Verify each licence from a primary source (LICENSE file or upstream page) and check the project is still maintained.
- 1. suggest: rank up to 3 candidates with fit (drop-in / good / partial / none), build-it effort (S / M / L / XL), lock-in and what I would lose. Update the matching entry in ~/src/foss-audit/data/curated.json (or add one), run the backend tests, commit it in that repo, then stop and ask me which one to install (or move on, for research-only items).
- 2. install: install the alternative I pick, migrate config/data where that is cheap, and show it actually running.
- must not: remove, disable or uninstall any of them; print their remove commands for me instead.
- must not: install anything before I have picked from step 1.
- optional: skip items whose curated entry is already settled and whose alternative is already installed; list them at the end instead.
## done
- every item has a curated.json entry with verified licences, committed in that repo with \`.venv/bin/python -m pytest -q\` green.
- every installable item I picked shows its alternative under \`alternative.installed\` in \`.venv/bin/python -m foss_audit.scan\`.
## verify
On this machine, from ~/src/foss-audit: \`.venv/bin/python -m foss_audit.scan | jq '.items[] | select(.verdict != "foss") | {id, alternative}'\`.
## known

### google-chrome (\`aur:google-chrome\`): research, suggest, install
- id: \`aur:google-chrome\`, source: aur, version: 5.2.0-1
- verdict: Non-free; evidence: custom:chrome
- licence: custom:chrome
- homepage: https://www.google.com/chrome
- required by: nothing
- curated alternatives: Chromium, Firefox (fit: Drop-in, build-it effort: XL · infeasible, why: a browser, lock-in: Google Sync); already installed: ungoogled-chromium-bin
- remove command: \`sudo pacman -Rns google-chrome\` (do not run it)

